Printable photo reconstruction worker

This image includes two MediaPipe models, each downloaded unmodified:

- the face landmarker, face_landmarker.task, from
  https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/face_landmarker/float16/1/face_landmarker.task
- the multiclass selfie segmenter, selfie_multiclass_256x256.tflite, from
  https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/image_segmenter/selfie_multiclass_256x256/float32/1/selfie_multiclass_256x256.tflite

Both are published by Google under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The
license text and MediaPipe's NOTICE are installed with the mediapipe Python
package in this image, under
/opt/recon/lib/python3*/site-packages/mediapipe-*.dist-info/licenses/.

OpenCV is built from the opencv-python 5.0.0.93 source distribution with only
its core and image processing modules, without FFmpeg or other media
libraries. It is under the Apache License, Version 2.0; its license is at
/opt/opencv-python/LICENSE-OpenCV.

The installed Python packages, including PyTorch and torchvision, carry their
own licenses in their .dist-info directories under
/opt/recon/lib/python3*/site-packages/.

The image contains no MICA, SMIRK, DECA or FLAME model files. Those are
obtained separately by the operator and mounted at run time.

Depth estimation follows the inference procedure of Marigold V2
(https://github.com/kpbm-ai/marigoldv2), published by Huawei Bayer Lab under
the Apache License, Version 2.0, and builds its networks from the Hugging
Face diffusers model definitions, also Apache-2.0. The image contains no
Qwen-Image-Edit-2509 or Marigold V2 weights; the operator downloads them,
converts them with convert_marigold.py and mounts the result at run time.

Object generation follows the network definitions and inference procedure of
Pixal3D (https://github.com/TencentARC/Pixal3D), copyright 2026 Tencent,
and of the TRELLIS.2 backbone it builds on
(https://github.com/microsoft/TRELLIS.2), copyright Microsoft Corporation,
both under the MIT License. Its feature upsampler follows NAF
(https://github.com/valeoai/NAF), published by valeo.ai under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. Its DINOv3 network is the Hugging Face transformers
definition, Apache-2.0. The image contains no Pixal3D, DINOv3, NAF or
BiRefNet weights; the operator downloads them and mounts them at run time.

Background removal uses BiRefNet's network definition, birefnet.py and
BiRefNet_config.py, downloaded unmodified from
https://huggingface.co/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet at revision
e2bf8e4460fc8fa32bba5ea4d94b3233d367b0e4 and installed under
/opt/printable/recon/vendor/birefnet/. Its Swin Transformer portion is
copyright 2021 Microsoft. It is published under the MIT License:

